course: dictionary
lesson: 3297
title: Eternal: forever, and more than one meaning
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. Look at the sentence around the word to decide which meaning fits. «Christians hope for eternal life with God» tells you that eternal means lasting for ever, without an end.
explain: Context can also show a different meaning. «His eternal complaining made the whole class groan» does not mean he complains for ever in a literal way. It means he complains so much it seems never to stop, and it is annoying. Ask yourself: what would fit here?
explain: Eternal can also mean always true or always there, as in «an eternal optimist», someone who always expects things to go well. Swap your meaning into the sentence to check that it still makes sense.
fact: Eternal means lasting for ever, without beginning or end.
fact: Eternal is an adjective. The adverb is eternally.
fact: «Eternal life» is a phrase used in religion lessons, where Christians believe it begins now and goes on after death.
fact: «The Eternal City» is a name for Rome.
fact: In everyday talk, eternal can mean seeming to go on for ever, often annoyingly, as in «his eternal complaining».
exercise: «Christians hope for eternal life with God.» What does eternal mean here? | Only for one special day | Hidden under the ground | Very short and quick | *Lasting for ever, without an end
exercise: «His eternal complaining made the whole class groan.» What does eternal suggest? | Always kind and cheerful | Lasting for ever in heaven | Sudden and surprising | *Seeming to go on for ever, often annoyingly
exercise: Ruby is «an eternal optimist». What does this tell you about Ruby? | Asleep most of the day | Always grumpy about the weather | *Always hopeful and expecting good things | Never seen in school
test: Copy one word from this sentence that means lasting for ever: «Christians believe eternal life starts now and continues after death.» | continues | believe | death | *eternal
test: Which word is the adverb form of eternal? | *eternally | endless | ageless | eternal
exam: What is «The Eternal City» a name for? | London | Athens | *Rome | Paris
